<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Süntel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">782</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxon-wars">Saxon Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Süntel was fought in 782 in the Süntel hills near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser">Weser</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>, when a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> army raised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/widukind">Widukind</a> destroyed a Frankish force that had been sent against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sorbs">Sorbs</a>. The defeat provoked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>'s harsh response, the massacre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verden">Verden</a>, in which according to the Royal Frankish Annals some 4,500 Saxons were beheaded.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-suntel.jpg" alt="Battle of the Süntel" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Tortuosa at German Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HohensteinS%C3%BCntel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 782 Saxons destroyed a Frankish army in the <b>Süntel</b> hills, and Charlemagne responded by having some 4,500 Saxons beheaded at Verden, according to the Royal Frankish Annals, though the number and nature of the event are debated.</blockquote><a href="/empire/saxons">Saxons · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
